        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(gateway): isolate live-event sweep assertion",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe full gateway test shard can leave unrelated stale run contexts in the process-global registry. The worker live-event test asserted the registry-wide sweep count was exactly one, so it failed deterministically when other stale contexts existed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAssert the target run context exists before the sweep and is gone afterward. This preserves the test's real contract: sweeping the target context forces the receiver to resync, without coupling the assertion to unrelated global state.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone. Test-only stabilization; production behavior unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/worker-environments/live-events.test.ts` — 4 files, 100 tests passed\n- `git diff --check`\n- Original PR CI run 29235392005 reproduced the stale-count mismatch twice: expected 1, received 3\n- Manual whole-path review: registry sweep, target lookup, receiver claim/resync, and adjacent tests",
